Below is the exact request you would send to VirusTotal to retrieve the **subdomain** relationships for `example.org`, limited to 10 results and starting from the cursor `abc`.  
(Replace `my_api` with your real API key.)

```http
GET https://www.virustotal.com/api/v3/domains/example.org/related?limit=10&cursor=abc&relationship_type=subdomains
Host: www.virustotal.com
x-apikey: my_api
```

---

### Expected Response Format

VirusTotal will return a JSON payload similar to this (the actual IDs will depend on the current data in VT):

```json
{
  "data": [
    {
      "id": "sub1.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": {
        "last_analysis_stats": { ... },
        ...
      },
      "relationships": { ... },
      "context_attributes": {
        "relationship_type": "subdomains"
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "sub2.example.org",
      "type": "domain",
      "attributes": { ... },
      "relationships": { ... },
      "context_attributes": {
        "relationship_type": "subdomains"
      }
    },
    ...
  ],
  "meta": {
    "continuation_cursor": "defghijklmnop",
    "pagination": { ... }
  }
}
```

---

### Extracted Output (IDs + Context Attributes)

Since you requested **only** the related object IDs and their context attributes, here’s the trimmed-down result you would receive after parsing the above JSON:

```json
[
  {
    "id": "sub1.example.org",
    "context_attributes": {
      "relationship_type": "subdomains"
    }
